ol verification, not root self-approval. See findingRegisterPath and originalReviewExportPath; historical Opus data is retained but new Opus approval is not required.\",\n        \"Owner batch is intentionally being stopped for proven time-allocation design defect, not treated as completed.0h lacks required PRIMARY repetitions;0j partial archived,0k\/0l not yet run. See priorCoverageBatchOutcome and coverage-interruption.json. Fix reqscale allocation\/ceiling or split while preserving hypothesis and minimum required repeats before your WHITE mise run all. Complete existing measurements remain preserved. Current root will terminate only this owned local experiment and confirm quiescence before measurement runner. Author may edit after owner exits; do not create a second writer\/experiment.\"\n      ],\n      \"currentRevision\": 13,\n      \"detailPaths\": [\"docs\/table-count-evidence.md\", \"docs\/probability-count.md\"],\n      \"findingRegisterPath\": \"results\/reviews\/finding-register.json\",\n      \"frontierDesignReview\": {\n        \"assessmentPath\": \"results\/reviews\/sol-frontier-assessment.json\",\n        \"log\": \"results\/reviews\/sol-frontier-run.log\",\n        \"resultPath\": \"results\/reviews\/sol-frontier-review.json\",\n        \"snapshot\": \"results\/reference\/20261107-frontier-design\",\n        \"status\": \"completed,rejected middle3\/low1 on immutable pre-fix design\",\n        \"workflow\": \"temp-table-count-frontier-sol\"\n      },\n      \"guidelinePath\": \"docs\/table-count-guideline.md\",\n      \"latestAccuracySteering\": {\n        \"additionalServicePriority\": \"Because actual100-column3%-target sampling exhausted the1s service budget in all6 no-small-index arms, include a minimal bounded100-column TDE under-load comparison at relaxed10% (plus matched control and existing3% evidence). Test whether reduced draws actually improve budget\/precision outcomes, rather than infer from static checkpoints.5% can be static if a full service factorial would add little. Split scripts within20min limits; avoid an exhaustive redundant factorial.\",\n        \"conditionMechanisms\": \"Distinguish effects on statistical accuracy, cost under a fixed budget, and freshness. Key-space sparsity\/cell-density variance affect sampling interval convergence; page-level row-size\/density heterogeneity, stats sample pages and staleness affect metadata error. A small index, cache, TDE, row width and MVCC mainly change read\/CPU\/time cost and therefore attainable precision within a fixed budget; they do not make a completed snapshotCOUNT approximate. Concurrent writes\/replica lag can change the represented time\/population and must not be conflated with estimator error. More sample pages\/ANALYZE does not guarantee monotonic accuracy and has separate maintenance impact.\",\n        \"implementation\": \"Root added isolated bench\/accuracy_frontier.py plus01c-ACCURACY-COST and01d-ACCURACY-SERVICE-100 (.versions8.4.13\/.encrypted\/.outputs). No active imported source was edited. Code is prepared, NOT DB-executed. Review\/fix these scripts rather than duplicate.01c uses seven fixtures xfive seeds x3targets, fullCOUNT paired comparisons, target-specific predeclared looks and same alpha.01d uses100-column TDE with control\/exact\/3%\/10%, index absent\/present, indexed\/nonindexed writes x3repeats=48arms.5% service is explicitly unmeasured; static includes it. Pure arithmetic verifies each first look can meet its target at zero variance; static closure includes new module and sampling dependencies. Both new wrappers honor the review-only aggregate guard (exit3, never success) and declare their required .outputs. Final all has no aggregate cap.\",\n        \"interpretation\": \"Compare accuracy, elapsed time, read volume and service impact rather than require only3%. Include exactCOUNT at0% error. Choose the most favorable method within the accepted error, freshness and service budget;10% is not an unconditional guarantee for arbitrary unknown tables.\",\n        \"newExperiment\": \"Review and run the isolated implementation named in implementation after the current owner ends. Retain hypotheses and proper confidence\/look allocation. Repair demonstrated issues or split if20min is insufficient; do not duplicate experiments or infer unobserved service effects.\",\n        \"reporting\": \"Give a compact condition-by-method comparison with accuracy\/freshness\/cost\/limitations and recommended paths. Distinguish interval target from realized error and from global confidence. Relaxed accuracy does not prove no service impact.\",\n        \"requiredComparison\": [\n          \"Metadata realized errors and freshness; no guaranteed error bound\",\n          \"Conditional cell sampling at3%,5%,10% relative-error targets with matched confidence, precision failures, realized error, runtime and read volume\",\n          \"ExactCOUNT runtime\/reads\/impact, including cases where a small index beats sampling\",\n          \"50\/100 columns,TDE,index presence,key gaps\/density skew,concurrent changes,MVCC and caches; separate measured from unmeasured\"\n        ],\n        \"userInstruction\": \"数%に収まらなければ10%程度でもよい。どの条件で精度がどれくらい上がる\/下がるかを知り、そのうえで最高精度でperformance最大の件数取得方法を知りたい。\"\n      },\n      \"modelPolicy\": \"User explicitly instructed on 2026-11-07: Riela must use GPT-6.1 Sol only. No Opus step or Opus approval is required.\",\n      \"originalReviewExportPath\": \"results\/reviews\/original-revision10-reviews.json\",\n      \"phaseControl\": \"After active coverage owner exits: author fixes code\/protocols, fixed lab-runner runs white-database mise run all (no aggregate skip budget,12h workflow ceiling,20min per requested script), integrate edits documentation only. Stop after3steps. Owner audits semantic completeness and unchanged final benchmark source, creates final-all-proof.json, then resumes two Sol review passes. Repeat all only if benchmark source\/configuration changes or 